121	---
122	
123	**How the verdict was reached:** This is `partial`, not `implemented`, because the ordinary NFT-result and cash-result paths genuinely allocate two independent buckets and permit full releases in either order, but an accepted, initially code-less sponsor recipient can later become a registered same-factory clone and trigger the payout-time rejection branch. It is not `contradicted` because every stable-recipient path works, the treasury remains independently releasable in the failing sponsor scenario, and the release functions do not cross-consume state. The failing path is source-visible and reachable without relying on missing quote-token behavior, so confidence is high.
